@base = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@annaEmail = anna@group.local
@bohdanEmail = bohdan@group.local
@password = User123!

### login Anna
# @name annaLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{annaEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### login Bohdan
# @name bohdanLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{bohdanEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### SQLi: payload is treated as text because backend uses parameterized queries
GET {{base}}/posts?search=' OR 1=1 --&sortBy=createdAt&order=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{annaLogin.response.body.data.token}}

### XSS: stored value is accepted as text, frontend renders it through textContent
# @name xssPost
POST {{base}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{annaLogin.response.body.data.token}}

{
  "title": "XSS перевірка",
  "category": "news",
  "body": "<img src=x onerror=alert('xss')><script>alert('xss')</script>"
}

### IDOR: Bohdan cannot read Anna's post
GET {{base}}/posts/{{xssPost.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bohdanLogin.response.body.data.token}}

### IDOR: Anna can read her own post
GET {{base}}/posts/{{xssPost.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{annaLogin.response.body.data.token}}

### IDOR: Bohdan cannot update Anna's post
PUT {{base}}/posts/{{xssPost.response.body.data.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{bohdanLogin.response.body.data.token}}

{
  "title": "Чужа зміна",
  "category": "question",
  "body": "Це має повернути 403."
}

### Headers and clean error shape
GET http://localhost:3000/unknown-route
Origin: http://localhost:5500
